---
import FrameworkLayout from '@/layouts/FrameworkLayout.astro';
---

<FrameworkLayout
  title="3D-X Framework | ChiroCandy"
  description="The 3D-X Framework gives chiropractors a simple execution model: Define your strategy, Deploy campaigns and assets, then eXamine results and refine what works."
  slug="3d-x-framework"
  heroTitle="3D-X Framework"
  heroAnswer="The 3D-X Framework is ChiroCandy's chiropractic marketing execution model. Define what you are building, Deploy it across ads and content, then eXamine performance so every dollar gets smarter."
  definition="A three-phase cycle for planning, launching, and improving chiropractic marketing without guessing or starting over each month."
  stages={[
    {
      title: 'What does Define mean in the 3D-X model?',
      answer:
        'Define is where you set goals, choose your ideal patient, and decide what success looks like before you spend on ads.',
      detail:
        'You clarify offer, budget, timeline, and key metrics. Define also covers competitive positioning and the message you will test. Skipping this step leads to scattered campaigns and unclear ROI.',
    },
    {
      title: 'What does Deploy cover for chiropractic marketing?',
      answer:
        'Deploy is the launch phase where strategy becomes live ads, landing pages, email flows, and content.',
      detail:
        'You turn Define outputs into assets patients can see and click. Deploy includes creative, targeting, tracking setup, and scheduling. Speed matters here, but only after Define gives you a clear brief.',
    },
    {
      title: 'What does eXamine do for practice growth?',
      answer:
        'eXamine is the review phase where you measure leads, cost per patient, and conversion rates, then adjust.',
      detail:
        'You look at ad performance, page behavior, and front-desk conversion. Winners get more budget. Weak angles get replaced. eXamine closes the loop back to Define so the next cycle starts with real data.',
    },
  ]}
  faqs={[
    {
      question: 'How often should a practice run the 3D-X cycle?',
      answer:
        'Run a full eXamine review every two to four weeks during active campaigns. Define only needs a deep refresh when goals, offers, or markets change.',
    },
    {
      question: 'Can Deploy happen before Define is finished?',
      answer:
        'You can launch fast, but without Define you will not know what to measure or fix. A short Define sprint prevents expensive rework in Deploy.',
    },
  ]}
  relatedServices={[
    { href: '/services/google-advertising/', label: 'Google Ads for Chiropractors' },
    { href: '/services/facebook-advertising/', label: 'Chiropractic Facebook Ads' },
    { href: '/services/web-design/', label: 'Chiropractic Web Design' },
  ]}
/>
